zdots-pages — reusable GitHub Pages + Wiki publisher for the just3ws systems.

One framework, every repo: renders a repo's curated docs (docs/wiki/*.md) into
a Jekyll site on a gh-pages worktree with a SHARED theme/nav (etc/pages/), and
optionally syncs the same pages to the repo's GitHub Wiki. Proven on zdots,
then applied to adots / vdots / my / phalanxduel / wwworkremote.

Fail-closed, outward-action discipline (mirrors zdots PHI doctrine):
  - Visibility guard: refuses to publish a PRIVATE repo to a PUBLIC Pages site
    unless --allow-private is passed explicitly. Public exposure is one-way.
  - `build`/`status` are local and reversible. `publish`/`wiki` only push the
    outward branch when --push is given; without it they stage and report.

Usage:
  zdots-pages status              # repo, visibility, page count, wiki state
  zdots-pages build               # render site into the gh-pages worktree (local)
  zdots-pages publish [--push]    # commit gh-pages; push only with --push
  zdots-pages wiki    [--push]    # sync docs/wiki → <repo>.wiki.git; push w/ --push
  zdots-pages init                # create the orphan gh-pages branch + worktree

Options:
  --repo DIR        operate on another repo (default: current git toplevel)
  --git-dir DIR     operate on a BARE repo by its git dir (e.g. ~/.homegit);
                    requires --wiki-src (no working tree to infer docs from)
  --wiki-src DIR    override the docs source dir (default <root>/docs/wiki)
  --worktree DIR    override the gh-pages worktree path
  --allow-private   permit publishing a private repo (you accept the exposure)
  --push            perform the outward push (publish/wiki)
  -h, --help        this help
.fi
